35,2,1,talk,Ryuji,,"The financial data is concerning. Transport costs fluctuate wildly depending on distance, and fixed-headcount lets create a high risk of deficits if members cancel.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"I've found that some options carry a massive administrative burden. Certain booking processes are incredibly rigid and time-consuming, and on-site duties can be grueling.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Minako,,"My findings suggest that the lack of cohesion is tied to the living arrangements. If we don't force shared living, the year-groups will remain isolated.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,I am concerned about the sleeping conditions. Some of the more affordable options seem to have very crowded rooms and strict rules that might hinder recovery.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Asuka,,"The risk of late cancellations is a serious issue. If we choose a whole-building let with non-refundable deposits, the remaining members will be unfairly penalized.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Asuka, exactly. We cannot afford to announce a price and then ask for more money later. We need a destination where the cost is predictable and stable.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, predictability in cost is good, but predictability in labor is also necessary. We cannot have organizers spending their entire camp in the kitchen.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Toshio, I understand the burden, but if we prioritize ease over interaction, we are failing the club's social health. We need a place that encourages togetherness.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, togetherness is valuable, but not if it comes at the cost of sleep. Eight people to a room with strict lights-out may lead to the same exhaustion as last year.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Asuka,,We should avoid options that rely on rigid headcount deposits. A flexible booking system is essential to ensure that the financial burden doesn't fall on a few people.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Ryuji,,"If we choose a local destination, we drastically reduce the transport risk. The data shows that distance is the primary driver of budget instability.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"I agree with reducing risk, but we must avoid any option that requires a lottery-style application or extensive manual labor on-site. The organizers need to train.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Minako,,"A local destination might be too familiar. To break the year-group barriers, we need an environment that removes them from their daily routine and forces them to rely on each other.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I am leaning toward options that offer more space per person. If the inland centers are too crowded, we should look for something that guarantees a better night's rest.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Asuka,,I am prioritizing the financial structure. Any option that allows for individual cancellations without affecting the group's flat fee is the only logical choice.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Ryuji,,"We must balance these needs, but the club account cannot sustain another deficit. I will vote for the option that minimizes financial volatility.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Toshio,,I will vote for the option that minimizes the administrative and labor burden on the organizers. We cannot sacrifice the training of the leadership.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Minako,,I will vote for the option that maximizes shared living and social interaction. The long-term health of the club depends on the members actually knowing each other.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will vote for the option that provides the most conducive environment for sleep and recovery. Training is useless if the members are too exhausted to perform.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Asuka,,I will vote for the option that ensures fair cost distribution and protects the members from paying for those who cancel.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
