60,3,1,talk,Ryuji,,Option B is the only choice that eliminates transport volatility and the risk of non-refundable deposits. It is the only financially safe option.,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Toshio,,"Option A is the most attractive from a labor perspective. The owner handles the meals, and it avoids the bureaucratic nightmare of the municipal lottery system in Option C.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Option C is the best for cohesion. Shared dormitories force interaction across year-groups, unlike Option B where people just go home or stay in separate rooms.","{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,Option A seems the most promising for rest. A guesthouse is likely to be quieter and more comfortable than the crowded dorms of Option C or the fragmented nature of Option B.,"{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Asuka,,"Option B is the only one that avoids the ""headcount risk."" In Option A and C, a late cancellation would likely leave the remaining members to cover the cost.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Ryuji,,"@Toshio, while Option A is easier for you, the transport costs to another prefecture are a huge gamble. We cannot risk the budget on a long-distance trip.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Ryuji, the cost of transport is a one-time expense. The cost of an organizer losing a month of evenings to a municipal application is a loss of productivity we can't afford.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Ryuji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Minako,,"@Asuka, the financial risk is manageable if we set a strict deadline for payment. But the social risk of Option B is catastrophic; it's not a camp, it's just more practice.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Asuka""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Minako, the ""shared"" nature of Option C's dorms is exactly what I fear. Eight people to a room is a recipe for sleep deprivation, which we saw last year.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Asuka,,"@Minako, a deadline doesn't solve the problem of non-refundable deposits. If the lodge requires a full payment upfront, the club account takes the hit, or the members do.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Ryuji,,Option B is the only rational choice. It removes the transport variable and the deposit risk entirely. We can use the saved money to improve the training quality.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Toshio,,"Option B is too fragmented. If we are going to put in the effort to organize a camp, it should be a dedicated environment. Option A provides that without the labor of Option C.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Minako,,Option C is the only one that addresses the core problem of the club's division. The shared dorms are a necessary catalyst for the members to actually bond.,"{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"I cannot support Option C. The risk of poor sleep is too high. Option A offers a dedicated environment and likely better sleeping conditions, which is essential for the final day's performance.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Asuka,,Option B is the only one that ensures no member is unfairly penalized for another's absence. It is the only fair way to handle the flat fee.,"{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Ryuji,,I will stick with Option B. The financial stability of the club must come first.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Toshio,,I will vote for Option A. It balances the need for a dedicated camp environment with a manageable workload for the organizers.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Minako,,I will vote for Option C. The social fragmentation of this club is a crisis that only a shared-living environment can solve.,"{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,I will vote for Option A. It provides the best chance for the members to get the rest they need to actually benefit from the training.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Asuka,,I will vote for Option B. Fairness in cost distribution and the elimination of cancellation risks are my primary concerns.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
